<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42125" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sabis</span></b> , is, m.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A river in Gallia Belgica</i>, now <i>the Sambre</i>, <i><span class="en">Caes. B. G. 2, 16</span></i>; <i><span class="en">2,
			18</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A river in Carmania</i>, <i><span class="en">Mel. 3, 8,
			4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 6, 23, 27, §
			107</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>A deity of the Sabœans</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 12,
				14, 32, § 63</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
